# hi im furina

_a systems programmer_

## languages

i love and constantly use [zig](https://ziglang.org/), and also have recently started using
[c99](https://www.open-std.org/jtc1/sc22/WG14/www/docs/n1256.pdf) a lot, but i also have
adequate experience with and occasionally use [golang](https://go.dev/) and very occasionally
[rust](https://rust-lang.org/).

i also have experience with other miscellaneous languages such as [python3](https://python.org/),
[typescript](https://www.typescriptlang.org/), [scss](https://sass-lang.com/) and frameworks
and libraries such as [tailwind](https://tailwindcss.com/), [svelte](https://svelte.dev/),
[sveltekit](https://svelte.dev/docs/kit/introduction) and [solidjs](https://solidjs.org/).

## work

im currently a volunteer pr reviewer at the [is-a.dev](https://is-a.dev) subdomain service.

### wip projects

- [affine](https://repo.ririna.net/dragsbruh/affine):
  a 2d motion graphics library/framework in zig, inspired by after effects
- [ztime](https://repo.ririna.net/dragsbruh/ztime):
  an efficient uptime tracker designed specifically for selfhosted stuff

### cool projects

- [wiretooth](https://codeberg.org/dragsbruh/wiretooth):
  a bluetooth transport proxy for wireguard
- [lumine](https://codeberg.org/dragsbruh/lumine):
  an x86_64/aarch64 UEFI bootloader written in zig
- [envidiyuh](https://codeberg.org/dragsbruh/envidiyuh):
  a fast runtime for markov chains in c
- [brainfucc](https://codeberg.org/dragsbruh/brainfucc):
  optimizing brainfuck compiler for assembly
- [lexyc](https://codeberg.org/dragsbruh/lexyc):
  compilers for the "xy" esoteric programming language

### miscellaneous projects

- [lain](https://codeberg.org/dragsbruh/lain):
  a tiny and fast http/1.1 server library written in zig
- [minimux](https://codeberg.org/dragsbruh/minimux):
  a tiny linux kernel + userspace experiment, primarily made to test lumine
- [ziggymirror](https://codeberg.org/dragsbruh/ziggymirror):
  a community mirror server for the zig programming language

### open source contributions

- [git.orangc.net/c/takina](https://git.orang.ci/c/takina):
  a discord bot written in python
- [github.com/is-a-dev](https://github.com/is-a-dev/register/):
  a subdomain service for developers

## interests

i really like a lot of stuff, but generally most of my likings can be classified into:

- os-dev: im like doing stuff from scratch, like _scratch_
- graphics: did a few stuff here and there with opengl
- open source: cool shit, communism at its finest
- networking: anything that involves two devices communicating
- [creatures of steel](https://devilmayquake.com/)

### setup

for my daily driver i love and use the [void linux](https://voidlinux.org/) distribution, along with
with the [niri](https://niri-wm.github.io/) window manager. i use [helix](https://helix-editor.com/)
to write code.

### home server

i have a server that i run. its not the most reliable but works fantastic and i love it. the server
also uses void linux and manages selfhosted services via runit. this very site, as of writing this,
is hosted on my home server, but i also selfhost these other services primarily for myself.

- <https://ci.ririna.net> - woodpecker ci
- <https://repo.ririna.net> - forgejo
- <https://copy.ririna.net> - copyparty
- <https://home.ririna.net> - glance
- <https://mirror.ririna.net> - mirrors for zig and (todo) xbps

